Upstream Hermes' turn-end fix for the Relay, backported unmodified onto
the pinned v0.22.5 (images/hermes/Dockerfile applies it at build; the
build fails unless it applies cleanly).

  02438db863e199431b85021806a3467b0c9324a4
    fix(gateway): give producer-admitted relay turns their typing and
    reactions back
  c49ecd58922bdce210f68e96dfbd07d11d1c6bd5
    fix(gateway): a cancel during the producer start hook releases its
    typing and bracket

Both from NousResearch/hermes-agent main (2026-10-28), after v0.22.5. Their
gateway/ changes only: the image carries no tests/. Without them a relayed
message's turn never sends the 👀/✅ bracket the bridge reads as its end
(docs/technical-debt-ledger.md, "The Hermes image carries upstream's
Relay turn-end fix"). Delete when the next Hermes release we adopt
includes both commits.

From 02438db863e199431b85021806a3467b0c9324a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Victor Kyriazakos <victor@rocketfueldev.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:43:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(gateway): give producer-admitted relay turns their
 typing and reactions back

A relay chat message has been admitted natively since the session authority shipped (e75bc52f50,
first released in 0.22.3; e3fdebbf87 moved it into gateway/relay/inbound_admission.py):
RelayAdapter._on_inbound commits it through admit_producer and the authority's drain runs it.
The typing refresh and on_processing_start/on_processing_complete only ever ran in
BasePlatformAdapter._process_message_background, which that path never enters. So a relay
message got no in-progress reaction, no typing / Slack "is working" status, and no outcome
reaction; only tool progress re-sent typing, so a turn without tools showed nothing. Slash
commands still go through handle_message and kept theirs.

The turn executor now brackets producer-admitted turns (relay and webhook deliveries; a messaging
admission's own adapter task already brackets it):

- admit_producer marks the event it commits; SessionAuthority._admitted records a freshly queued
  row in the commit's own tracked task. A re-send of a row already running or settled is not
  marked again, and a cancelled queued row drops its mark (_settle_cancelled).
- execute_admission opens the bracket when the row starts executing, not when it commits: a
  message queued behind a running turn is acknowledged when it runs, as the in-band queue does
  (run_turn_followup_ack) and as 0.22.2's drain task did. It starts the adapter typing refresh
  with the event's thread metadata and runs on_processing_start.
- Typing lives as long as execution and stops before the reply is sent (#117300 pauses it there).
- The outcome is reported once: an interrupted turn as CANCELLED and a failed one (exception, or a
  failed result) as FAILURE when execution ends; a completed one after settlement, from the
  reply's send in deliver_settled (deliver_response now reports whether it delivered), or as
  FAILURE when settlement dropped the reply.
- Adapters that render neither typing nor processing hooks (webhook) get no bracket; scheduled
  wakes and heartbeats are not producer admissions, so they stay silent.

pre_gateway_dispatch still fires once at admission, admission stays off the transport reader and
the ACK semantics are unchanged: the bracket lives entirely on the execution side.
